,0));\ndraw((23,20)--(47,20)--(50,0)--(47,-20)--(21,-20));\ndraw((23,20)--(26,0)--(23,-20));\ndraw((31,20)--(34,0)--(31,-20));\ndraw((39,20)--(42,0)--(39,-20));\ndraw((39,21)--(39,25));\ndraw((47,21)--(47,25));\ndraw((39,23)--(47,23));\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-3,20),NW);\nlabel(\"$B$\",(47,20),NE);\nlabel(\"$C$\",(50,0),E);\nlabel(\"$D$\",(47,-20),SE);\nlabel(\"$E$\",(-3,-20),SW);\nlabel(\"$F$\",(0,0),W);\nlabel(\"20'\",(43,23),N);\nlabel(\"62'\",(49,10),E);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"7a34714dd2e3263ab8cafce5a5896ace6c470b2b428e577071a5eb4945cbf613"},"seconds":20.706968545913696,"seed":41721447200382774,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem step by step, we need to understand the structure of the hexagon $ABCDEF$ formed by the parallelograms and the given dimensions of the parallelograms.\n\n1. **Recognize the structure and dimensions:**\n   - Each parallelogram has sides of lengths 62 feet and 20 feet.\n   - The hexagon is formed by arranging these parallelograms in a chevron pattern.\n\n2. **Identify the sides of the hexagon:**\n   - The hexagon is symmetric and each side of the hexagon is formed by the longer side of the parallelogram (62 feet) or the shorter side of the parallelogram (20 feet).\n   - Given the pattern, we can see that the hexagon has three sides of 62 feet and three sides of 20 feet.\n\n3. **Calculate the perimeter:**\n   - The perimeter of the hexagon is the sum of the lengths of all its sides.\n   - There are three sides of 62 feet each and three sides of 20 feet each.\n   - Therefore, the perimeter \\( P \\) is calculated as:\n     \\[\n     P = 3 \\times 62 + 3 \\times 20\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     P = 186 + 60\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     P = 246 \\text{ feet}\n     \\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\) is \\(\\boxed{246}\\) feet."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{246}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
